; Tutorial_5_Web_Address.inix -- a web address, sound only, with context from the page.
[about]
Title=5 - A Web Address, Sound Only
Intro=A lecture on YouTube becomes one described MP3, a quarter the size of the video, with the page's own title guiding the descriptions.
Setup=HomerScribe is installed, with Ollama. A YouTube address is on the clipboard.
Homework=Give HomerScribe the address of a playlist. It says "Processing 3 of 9" as it goes, and each film gets its own folder.

[step]
Say=A lecture on YouTube, an hour of slides and a speaker. I do not need the video; I need to know what the slides say, and I want one file I can put on my phone.
Key=
Hear=

[step]
Say=Alt plus Control plus H opens the dialog, in Source paths as always.
Key=Alt+Control+H
Hear=HomerScribe dialog
Hear=Source paths: edit, https colon slash slash www dot youtube dot com slash watch question mark v equals 3 f 31 o u f q F S M

[step]
Say=Control plus A selects the sample address, and Control plus V pastes mine over it.
Key=Control+A
Hear=selected https colon slash slash www dot youtube dot com slash watch question mark v equals 3 f 31 o u f q F S M

[step]
Say=Control plus V.
Key=Control+V
Hear=
Note=The reader is silent on a paste. Press Insert plus Up Arrow to read the line if you want to check it.

[step]
Say=Silence on a paste is normal. Now the boxes. Alt plus D, Describe. Alt plus A, Audio only, A for Audio. Alt plus W, Web context, W for Web.
Key=Alt+D
Hear=Describe video check box, checked, Alt plus D

[step]
Say=Alt plus A.
Key=Alt+A
Hear=Audio only check box, checked, Alt plus A
Note=Audio only produces one described dot m p 3: the film's own sound with the descriptions mixed in, and no video. It is quicker to make and a quarter the size.

[step]
Say=Alt plus W.
Key=Alt+W
Hear=Web context check box, checked, Alt plus W
Note=Web context reads the page's title and description first, so the model knows it is looking at a lecture on, say, tax law, and describes the slides as slides rather than guessing.

[step]
Say=Three boxes checked. Enter.
Key=Enter
Hear=HomerScribe, working
Hear=Initializing, Downloading Introduction to Estate Planning, Lecture 4
Pause=1

[step]
Say=It named the lecture from the page. That title is what Web context gives the model. Let me verify the window while it works, with Insert T.
Key=Insert+T
Hear=HomerScribe, describing 17 of 88

[step]
Say=Describing seventeen of eighty eight. The title carries the progress, so Insert T is all it takes to check on a long run from another window. I will let it finish.
Key=
Hear=Done. Introduction to Estate Planning, Lecture 4
Hear=HomerScribe results dialog
Hear=One source done. Took 22 minutes. Introduction to Estate Planning, Lecture 4: 88 descriptions, 58 minutes. C colon backslash Users backslash Jamal backslash Videos backslash Introduction to Estate Planning Lecture 4. Log of this run: C colon backslash Users backslash Jamal backslash Videos backslash Introduction to Estate Planning Lecture 4 backslash HomerScribe dot log.
Hear=OK button
Pause=1

[step]
Say=Enter presses OK. The folder holds described dot m p 3, one file with the lecture and its descriptions, and described dot m d to read.
Key=Enter
Hear=HomerScribe dialog
Hear=Source paths: edit
Note=OK closes the results box and focus returns to the dialog, controls enabled again, ready for the next job.
